     "body": "<p><span class=\"error\">&#91;Followup from Sourceforge Tracker&#93;</span><br/>\nFollowup Submitter: sjw46<br/>\nLogged In: YES <br/>\nuser_id=1709161<br/>\nOriginator: YES</p>\n\n<p>Normally, API-M methods that do object modification will result in a new audit<br/>\nrecord in the object.  This is true for all component (datastream and<br/>\ndisseminator) methods, but in the case of the following methods, the logMessage<br/>\nis not recorded anywhere:</p>\n\n<ul class=\"alternate\" type=\"square\">\n\t<li>ingestObject</li>\n\t<li>modifyObject</li>\n\t<li>purgeObject</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<p>Note that for purgeObject, it makes no sense to put the audit record in the<br/>\nobject.  Something else needs to be done, like writing it to the system log.</p>",
     "created": "12/Mar/07 5:27 PM",
     "id": "10083",
     "jsdPublic": true,
